{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DOMRange","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" boundary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" boundary point.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element (this typically depends on the mechanism from which the DOM Range instance originates,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for example when obtaining the currently-selected document fragment using the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"window.selection"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"API). In the case of a DOM text node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position within the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"character data. In the case of a DOM element node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that designates a child text node."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" field is optional. When only the start field is specified, the domRange object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"represents a “collapsed” range that has identical ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" boundary points.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"https:\/\/github.com\/readium\/architecture\/blob\/master\/models\/locators\/extensions\/html.md#the-domrange-object","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Point"],"title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(json:warnings:)","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(start:end:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/jsonObject"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONObjectEncodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueDecodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueEncodable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/readiumshared\/domrange"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ReadiumShared"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"DOMRange","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DOMRange","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:13ReadiumShared8DOMRangeV"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This construct enables a serializable representation of a DOM Range."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc: